Subject: [PATCH 1/4] RISC-V: Implement riscv_macro_fusion_pair_p for ARC-V
 RHX-100 series.

#FIXME after https://github.com/foss-for-synopsys-dwc-arc-processors/gcc/pull/298 is merged
Add the RHX-100 macro-op fusion cases to the table in riscv-fusion.cc
and enable them from the tune's fusible_ops field.  riscv_fuse_bfext and
riscv_fuse_lui_ld were already there; this adds the rest.

Pairs that compete with adjacent load/store (ls-update, lui-st,
li-store) bail out when the next insn is a better adjacent memop
candidate.  Those, plus adjacent load/store themselves, wait until after
reload.

Fused_MAC only matches when the product is rs1 of the add:
  mul rd,...; add rd,rd,rs

I1->I2 means fusion only in that order; I1<->I2 means the two
instructions are interchangeable with regards to order.

  RISCV_FUSE_MULT_ADD       (riscv_fuse_mult_add, I1->I2)
      I1: mul rd,...; I2: add rd,rd,rs3 reading the mul result in rd
      (on RV64, mulw+addw with the result sign-extended to DImode).
  RISCV_FUSE_LI_BRANCH      (riscv_fuse_li_branch, I1->I2)
      I1: li rd; I2: conditional branch that uses rd.
  RISCV_FUSE_LI_STORE       (riscv_fuse_li_store, I1->I2)
      I1: li rt; I2: store of rt.
  RISCV_FUSE_LUI_ST         (riscv_fuse_lui_st, I1<->I2)
      I1/I2: lui and store.
  RISCV_FUSE_LUI_LD         (riscv_fuse_lui_ld, I1->I2)
      I1: lui rd; I2: load using rd as base and destination.
  RISCV_FUSE_LUI_LD_REV     (riscv_fuse_lui_ld_rev, I1->I2)
      I1: load; I2: lui with a destination distinct from the load.
  RISCV_FUSE_LS_UPDATE      (riscv_fuse_ls_update, I1<->I2)
      I1/I2: load or store with an addi that updates the access base.
  RISCV_FUSE_BFEXT          (riscv_fuse_bfext, I1->I2)
      I1: slli rd,rs; I2: srli rd,rd (bitfield extract).
  RISCV_FUSE_ADJACENT_LOAD  (riscv_fuse_adjacent_load, I1<->I2)
      I1/I2: two loads, same base, offsets |off1-off2| == XLEN/8.
  RISCV_FUSE_ADJACENT_STORE (riscv_fuse_adjacent_store, I1<->I2)
      I1/I2: two stores, same base, offsets |off1-off2| == XLEN/8.

